From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:53:38 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add missing runtime deps, requirements-dev.txt, and a real CI
 workflow

- requirements.txt: add prometheus-client, prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator
  and rq. src/main.py imports the first at module top and history_queue
  imports rq, so the Docker image (which installs only requirements.txt)
  would crash on startup with ModuleNotFoundError.
- requirements-dev.txt: pytest, fakeredis+lupa, testcontainers, alembic,
  psycopg[binary]; includes requirements.txt.
- Remove root test_unit_pipeline_matching.py: a strict subset of
  tests/unit/test_pipeline_matching.py (5 fewer tests) that depended on a
  fixture not defined for it, so it never ran.
- CI: replace the integration-only workflow. Job 1 runs unit + integration
  against a postgres:16 service via TEST_DATABASE_URL. Job 2 installs
  redis-server, starts a master (6390) + Sentinel (26379), and runs the
  concurrency and failover tiers. Both installed from requirements-dev.txt.

Verified locally with the same commands: 73 unit + 18 integration + 6
concurrency + 5 failover = 102 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgSuF1U5kDij8YZySminES
